  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As follow up to the activities previously undertaken, it is envisaged during the biennium 2024-2025 to support the Somali Chamber of Commerce and Industry (SCCI) under CPO SOM801 to develop a multi-year strategic plan, which puts in value their socio-economic value and standing, and which also addresses the stated needs of more structured lobbying and advocacy and continued institutional capacity strengthening. The main strategy will focus on undertaking activities to strengthen the organization&#x2019;s overall involvement in policy debate especially in the social sphere as they were previously mostly operating in the economic sphere. As part of this activity the organization&#x2019;s capacity will also be strengthened to represent the Somali private sectors interests within the overall UN System, as propagated by the recent UN reform. 
Under this CPO the development of a new strategic plan and implementation with focus on advocacy meets the criteria so that the CPO will be TARGET on 2.1.1. and should give a reportable result. The interventions under this CPO are supported through RBTC resources allocations from ACT/EMP and CO-Addis Ababa.</narrative>
  </description>
